30,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"As I feared, our history is a mixed bag. Some structural work holds, but the greenery is often neglected to death due to poor contracting.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The situation is worse than I thought. Only two firms are tendering for earth-moving, and they've already flagged subsoil risks. Any complex dig will likely cause delays.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,Oh no! I found out that plants are way more expensive to keep than pavement! But the habitat fund only pays for the plants! We're in a trap!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The staffing situation is critical. The roll has dropped from eighteen to seven. We are relying on a skeleton crew and a few overstretched volunteers.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data confirms my concerns. The park is a transit corridor for commuters, and the drainage is failing. We cannot afford a design that blocks paths or adds water stress.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, your discovery explains my findings. The trees died because the budget for ""planting"" didn't include ""keeping them alive."" We must avoid high-maintenance greenery.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, if the drainage is already failing and the soil is clay-heavy, any plan with deep foundations or heavy water features is a recipe for disaster.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! If we pick a plan with tons of fancy gardens, the city will be broke in three years! We need something that is easy to clean and cheap to keep!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, it is not just about money. Even if we have the funds, we have no people. Seven staff members cannot manage a complex botanical garden.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"We must prioritize hard-wearing surfaces and natural drainage. If the commuters are already cutting corners, we should design the paths where they actually walk.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I suggest we look for a candidate that favors durability over aesthetics. A simple, well-built plaza is better than a dying forest.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We need a plan that minimizes earth-moving. If we stick to the surface or use light structures, we avoid the clay risks and the contractor shortage.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But we have to use the habitat fund! If we don't plant things, we lose the money! We just need plants that don't need a million dollars to survive!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, we need plants that don't need a million hours of labor. We cannot add more to the rota. We need low-maintenance, native species that require zero daily care.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"The heat readings show the site is a heat island. We need shade, but it must be provided by hardy trees, not delicate shrubs that will wither in August.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are in agreement. We need a plan that is structurally conservative, labor-light, and avoids the vanity of high-maintenance landscaping.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Precisely. If the plan requires extensive digging or specialized contractors, it will drift past the deadline. Simplicity is our only safety.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'll agree to a simpler plan, as long as it doesn't leave us with a massive bill! I'm still worried about those long-term accounts!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will support any plan that does not assume the existence of a phantom workforce. If it requires daily pruning or weeding, it is a failure.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,We must ensure the final choice respects the commuters' paths and the soil's inability to drain. Let us evaluate the candidates with these constraints in mind.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
