60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan B and C are far too ambitious. Given the history of dead trees and the current labor shortage, a ""Woodland"" or ""Wetland"" will become a swamp of weeds.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I strongly object to Plan C. Reshaping drainage into ponds requires massive earth-moving in clay soil. With only two firms available, that project will never finish.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Plan B and C use the habitat fund, but they'll cost a fortune to maintain! Plan A is mostly pavement, which is cheap to keep, but we lose the funding!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Plan B and C are impossible. Seven staff members cannot manage a woodland or a wetland. Plan D requires constant maintenance of courts and facilities. Plan A is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,Plan C is a disaster waiting to happen given the current drainage failures. Plan B ignores the commuter paths. Plan A provides the hard surfaces the people actually use.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, the habitat fund is a trap if it forces us into a maintenance nightmare. I would rather have a functional plaza than a dead forest.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Asuka, I agree. Plan A minimizes the need for deep digging and specialized earth-moving. It is the only plan that is actually feasible within the current contractor market.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,"But what about the greenery? If we go with Plan A, can we add some hardy, low-cost plants around the edges to keep some of the habitat fund?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,As long as those plants are native and self-sustaining. Plan A's focus on a paved square means the staff can focus on cleaning rather than constant gardening.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Plan A also addresses the heat island effect if the shade structures are well-placed. It respects the commuter flow by providing open, firm ground.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan A is the most honest proposal. It doesn't pretend we have a workforce we don't possess, nor does it ignore the failures of our past landscaping.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"From a construction standpoint, Plan A is the only safe bet. No massive excavations, no risky soil reshaping, and a timeline that the local firms can actually meet.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm still a bit sad about the fund, but I'm more scared of the budget deficit! Plan A is the safest for the city's wallet in the long run.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,It is the only plan that doesn't break the staff. We cannot ask seven people to do the work of eighteen. Plan A is the only sustainable option for the rota.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"The physical reality of the site—the drainage, the heat, and the commuters—all point to Plan A. It is the only design that works with the ground rather than fighting it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It is rare that we find such swift consensus. Logic has led us to the only viable conclusion. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Feasibility and risk management must come first. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,"Okay! For the sake of the budget and the future, I'm in! Plan A it is!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will not support any plan that ignores the labor crisis. Plan A is the only one that is realistic. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,The facts are clear. Plan A aligns with the usage patterns and the environmental constraints of the site. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
